  <guid>https://williamlfang.github.io/2026-11-14-ssh-linux-mint-lid-closed/</guid>
  <description><![CDATA[<div class="featured-image"><img loading="eager" src="https://williamlfang.github.io/2026-11-14-ssh-linux-mint-lid-closed/featured-image.png" alt="Keep SSH reachable with a closed lid on Linux Mint" title="Keep SSH reachable with a closed lid on Linux Mint" referrerpolicy="no-referrer"/></div><p>My Linux Mint notebook accepted SSH connections while its lid was open, but became unreachable when I shut it. The connection command was unchanged:</p>
<div class="highlight" id="id-1"><div class="chroma">
<table class="lntable"><tr><td class="lntd">
<pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code><span class="lnt">1
</span></code></pre></td>
<td class="lntd">
<pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="line"><span class="cl">ssh william@127.0.0.1 -p <span class="m">62223</span></span></span></code></pre></td></tr></table>
</div>
</div><p>The relevant setting was not in <code>sshd_config</code>. <strong>Cinnamon was configured to suspend the notebook when the lid closed, even on AC power.</strong> I changed just the AC lid action, leaving the battery policies alone.</p>]]></description>
